<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andeca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 584–585</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andeca was the last ruler of the Suebic kingdom in Gallaecia. In 584 he overthrew the young king Eboric, son of Miro, and married Miro's widow. In 585 the Visigothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liuvigild">Leovigild</a> invaded, deposed him and had him tonsured, ending the independent Suebic kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andeca.jpg" alt="Andeca" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Museo Arqueológico Nacional · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moneda_Audeca.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
